// A host that holds a NUL byte is a runtime error for connect
// (spec/05-stdlib.md, Strings the host reads): getaddrinfo() reads the name
// only up to the NUL, so the call would connect to a different host. The
// listener makes that difference visible: a consumer that truncates the String
// connects to it, and the program then exits 0.
// STATUS: error
// CHECK: before
// COVERS: host-string connect
print "before";
var l = listen("127.0.0.1", 0);
connect("127.0.0.1" + chr(0) + "tail", l.port());
